ileges within the container","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a container privilege escalation flaw was found in certain multi-cloud object gateway core images. this issue stems from the /etc/passwd file being created with group-writable permissions during build time. in certain conditions, an attacker who can execute commands within an affected container, even as a non-root user, can leverage their membership in the root group to modify the /etc/passwd file. this could allow the attacker to add a new user with any arbitrary uid, including uid 0, leading to full root privileges within the container"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Openshift Data Foundation 4.22","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift data foundation 4.22"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-276","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-276"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-8766","predicate":"vendor","object":"Red Hat","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"assigner","object":"Go","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-05-22T15:01:21.462Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-05-22t15:01:21.462z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-11T12:09:11.607Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-11t12:09:11.607z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"description","object":"The ToASCII and ToUnicode functions incorrectly accept Punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ASCII-only label. For example, ToUnicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error. This behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. For example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ASCII hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". If that program subsequently converts the ASCII hostname to Unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the Unicode name \"example.com\".","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"the toascii and tounicode functions incorrectly accept punycode-encoded labels that decode to an ascii-only label. for example, tounicode(\"xn--example-.com\") incorrectly returns the name \"example.com\" rather than an error. this behavior can lead to privilege escalation in programs using the idna package. for example, a program which performs privilege checks on the ascii hostname may reject \"example.com\" but permit \"xn--example-.com\". if that program subsequently converts the ascii hostname to unicode, it will inadvertently permits access to the unicode name \"example.com\"."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"product","object":"net/http","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"net/http"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"product","object":"net/http/internal/http2","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"net/http/internal/http2"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"product","object":"golang.org/x/net/idna","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/net/idna"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-1289","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-1289"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"vendor","object":"Go standard library","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go standard library"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39821","predicate":"vendor","object":"golang.org/x/net","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/net"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"assigner","object":"Go","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-05-22T02:31:26.883Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-05-22t02:31:26.883z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-11T12:09:11.238Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-11t12:09:11.238z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"description","object":"When an SSH server authentication callback returned PartialSuccessError with non-nil Permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. Returning non-nil Permissions with PartialSuccessError now results in a connection error.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"when an ssh server authentication callback returned partialsuccesserror with non-nil permissions, those permissions were silently discarded, potentially dropping certificate restrictions such as force-command after a second factor succeeded. returning non-nil permissions with partialsuccesserror now results in a connection error."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"product","object":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-863","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-863"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39828","predicate":"vendor","object":"golang.org/x/crypto","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"assigner","object":"Go","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-05-22T02:31:27.324Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-05-22t02:31:27.324z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-11T12:09:07.529Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-11t12:09:07.529z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"description","object":"The RSA and DSA public key parsers did not enforce size limits on key parameters. A crafted public key with an excessively large modulus or DSA parameter could cause several minutes of CPU consumption during signature verification. This could be triggered by unauthenticated clients during public key authentication. RSA moduli are now limited to 8192 bits, and DSA parameters are validated per FIPS 186-2.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"the rsa and dsa public key parsers did not enforce size limits on key parameters. a crafted public key with an excessively large modulus or dsa parameter could cause several minutes of cpu consumption during signature verification. this could be triggered by unauthenticated clients during public key authentication. rsa moduli are now limited to 8192 bits, and dsa parameters are validated per fips 186-2."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"product","object":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-1176","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-1176"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39829","predicate":"vendor","object":"golang.org/x/crypto","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"assigner","object":"Go","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-05-22T02:31:27.208Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-05-22t02:31:27.208z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-11T12:08:58.288Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-11t12:08:58.288z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"description","object":"A malicious SSH peer could send unsolicited global request responses to fill an internal buffer, blocking the connection's read loop. The blocked goroutine could not be released by calling Close(), resulting in a resource leak per connection. Unsolicited global responses are now discarded.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a malicious ssh peer could send unsolicited global request responses to fill an internal buffer, blocking the connection's read loop. the blocked goroutine could not be released by calling close(), resulting in a resource leak per connection. unsolicited global responses are now discarded."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"product","object":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-833","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-833"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39830","predicate":"vendor","object":"golang.org/x/crypto","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"assigner","object":"Go","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-05-22T02:31:26.660Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-05-22t02:31:26.660z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-11T12:09:11.654Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-11t12:09:11.654z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"description","object":"When adding a key to a remote agent constraint extensions such as restrict-destination-v00@openssh.com were not serialized in the request. Destination restrictions were silently stripped when forwarding keys, allowing unrestricted use of the key on the remote host. The client now serializes all constraint extensions. Additionally, the in-memory keyring returned by NewKeyring() now rejects keys with unsupported constraint extensions instead of silently ignoring them.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"when adding a key to a remote agent constraint extensions such as restrict-destination-v00@openssh.com were not serialized in the request. destination restrictions were silently stripped when forwarding keys, allowing unrestricted use of the key on the remote host. the client now serializes all constraint extensions. additionally, the in-memory keyring returned by newkeyring() now rejects keys with unsupported constraint extensions instead of silently ignoring them."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"product","object":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-281","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-281"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"published"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39832","predicate":"vendor","object":"golang.org/x/crypto","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"golang.org/x/crypto"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39835","predicate":"assigner","object":"Go","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"go"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39835","predicate":"date-published","object":"2026-05-22T02:31:26.982Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-05-22t02:31:26.982z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39835","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-09-11T12:09:05.121Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-09-11t12:09:05.121z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39835","predicate":"description","object":"SSH servers which use CertChecker as a public key callback without setting IsUserAuthority or IsHostAuthority could be caused to panic by a client presenting a certificate. CertChecker now returns an error instead of panicking when these callbacks are nil.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"ssh servers which use certchecker as a public key callback without setting isuserauthority or ishostauthority could be caused to panic by a client presenting a certificate. certchecker now returns an error instead of panicking when these callbacks are nil."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-39835","predicate":"p